                "description": "FFWRLX\n\nThe National Weather Service in Charleston has issued a\n\n* Flash Flood Warning for...\nNortheastern Braxton County in north central West Virginia...\nEast Central Gilmer County in north central West Virginia...\nSouthwestern Barbour County in northeastern West Virginia...\nNorthern Upshur County in northeastern West Virginia...\nCentral Lewis County in northern West Virginia...\n\n* Until 130 AM EDT.\n\n* At 1028 PM EDT, Doppler radar indicated thunderstorms producing\nheavy rain across the warned area. Between 1 and 3 inches of rain\nhave fallen. Flash flooding is ongoing or expected to begin\nshortly.\n\nHAZARD...Flash flooding caused by thunderstorms.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Flash flooding of small creeks and streams, urban areas,\nhighways, streets and underpasses as well as other poor\ndrainage and low-lying areas.\n\n* Some locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nBuckhannon, Weston, Audra State Park, Stonewall Jackson,\nBurnsville, Sand Fork, Horner, Lorentz, Walkersville, French Creek,\nSand Run, Hodgesville, Overhill, Century, Volga and Stouts Mills.\n\nThis includes the following highways...\nInterstate 79 between mile markers 74 and 101. Route 33 between mile\nmarkers 1 and 7...and between mile markers 15 and 17.",
